        </div>
        <ol class="how howto__steps">
          <li><b>01</b><strong>Open and keep it dry</strong><span>Peel the seal back, keep the pouch upright, and press it fully closed again afterwards.</span></li>
          <li><b>02</b><strong>Measure your serving</strong><span>The label serving is <b>1 teaspoon (2.5&nbsp;g)</b>, which carries 30&nbsp;mg of mitragynine. A gram scale is still the most accurate way to hit it, spoons vary, and the label is the guide.</span></li>
          <li><b>03</b><strong>Stir into something with body</strong><span>Water, juice, or a smoothie, stir until it’s evenly green. It won’t fully dissolve; it’s milled leaf, so it settles. Give it another stir before you finish.</span></li>
          <li><b>04</b><strong>Start low, then wait</strong><span>Give it time before deciding anything. You can always take more later; you can’t take less.</span></li>
        </ol>
