  {% comment %} ---------- FAQ: powder-specific ---------- {% endcomment %}
  <section class="belowfold belowfold--rule" aria-labelledby="d2p-faq-{{ section.id }}">
    <div class="belowfold__inner belowfold__inner--narrow">
      <p class="steplabel">Straight answers</p>
      <h2 class="belowfold__title" id="d2p-faq-{{ section.id }}">Powder questions.</h2>
      <div class="faq">
        <details><summary>How do people take loose powder?</summary><p>Most weigh it and wash it down with water or juice, or stir it into something with body. It does not dissolve, it’s milled leaf, so it will settle. Taste is earthy and bitter; that’s the format, not a flaw.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Why is there no subscription on powder?</summary><p>Because we haven’t finished the economics on it. Rather than show a plan we can’t honour at renewal, powder is one-time only for now. Gummies have a live subscription today.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Is powder stronger than the gummies?</summary><p>It isn’t a fair comparison and we won’t pretend otherwise. Powder is whole leaf measured in grams; gummies are a measured 35 mg of mitragynine each; capsules are an extract. Treat each as its own thing and start low on any of them.</p></details>
        <details><summary>How long does a pouch last?</summary><p>The label serving is 1 teaspoon (2.5&nbsp;g), so the 250&nbsp;g pouch holds <b>100 servings</b> and the 100&nbsp;g pouch holds <b>40</b>. How long that lasts depends on how often you reach for it.</p></details>
        <details><summary>How should I store it?</summary><p>Sealed, dry, out of sunlight. The pouch is resealable, press the seal fully closed and keep it away from steam and heat.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Who shouldn’t take it?</summary><p>Anyone under 21, anyone pregnant or nursing, and anyone on medication without talking to their clinician first. We don’t ship to 16 states, <a href="{{ url_ship }}">check yours</a>.</p></details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

